=== 1. Input optimization ===
x is not a parameter: true
the default stepped set is the weight alone: true
step 1: checksum over x's gradient = 4 + 12: true
step 1: global norm over x's gradient = sqrt 160: true
step 1: x moved by lr * 2 w x: true
x after step 1: 0.5000 0.5000
step 2: x moved by the gradient taken at the updated x: true
x after step 2: 0.2500 0.1250
the weight was not stepped: true
the checkpoint state set holds x, carried by the routine that steps it: true
=== 2. Accumulation ===
cycle 1 x gradient: 10.0000 7.5000
cycle 1: x's gradient is the mean of its micro-step gradients: true
cycle 1: w's gradient is the mean of its micro-step gradients: true
the default reset zeroes x's gradient: true
the default reset zeroes w's gradient: true
cycle 2: x's gradient starts clean: true
cycle 2: w's gradient starts clean: true
=== 3. Fetch-defined leaf ===
sgd_update ~params:{x} refuses the fetch-defined leaf: true
the refusal names the leaf: true
the refusal names Operation.init as the fix: true
the refusal carries the leaf: true
bypassed: step 1 moves x by lr * 2 w x: true
bypassed: step 2 lands where step 1 did -- the forward re-fetched x: true
the data-backed twin is accepted: true
data-backed: step 1 moves x by lr * 2 w x: true
data-backed: step 2 moves x by the gradient taken at the updated x: true
